---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sizing Standards Reference — SizeToolsHub"
  description="Learn about the international sizing standards behind SizeToolsHub's conversion tools: ISO 216, ISO 9407, ASTM, EN 13402, and more."
  canonicalUrl="https://sizetoolshub.com/about/standards/"
>
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-20">

    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-16">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline-soft mb-6 shadow-2xs">
        <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>
        <span class="text-xs font-semibold text-ink">Reference</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-6" style="line-height: 1.08;">
        Sizing Standards
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-text-muted font-light leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        All conversion data on SizeToolsHub is derived from official international standards. Here's a reference guide to the standards bodies and specifications behind our tools.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Standards Grid -->
    <section class="mb-20">
      <div class="space-y-6">

        <!-- ISO 216 -->
        <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-canvas border border-hairline-soft">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
            <div>
              <span class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent text-[11px] font-semibold mb-2">ISO Standard</span>
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">ISO 216 — Paper Sizes</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="text-3xl flex-shrink-0">📄</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
            ISO 216 defines the international standard for paper sizes, based on the square root of 2 aspect ratio (√2 ≈ 1.4142). This ensures that when a sheet is folded in half, the resulting piece maintains the same proportions.
          </p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 mb-4">
            {[
              { size: 'A0', dims: '841 × 1189 mm' },
              { size: 'A1', dims: '594 × 841 mm' },
              { size: 'A2', dims: '420 × 594 mm' },
              { size: 'A3', dims: '297 × 420 mm' },
              { size: 'A4', dims: '210 × 297 mm' },
              { size: 'A5', dims: '148 × 210 mm' },
              { size: 'A6', dims: '105 × 148 mm' },
              { size: 'B4', dims: '250 × 353 mm' },
            ].map((p) => (
              <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft text-center">
                <div class="font-bold text-ink text-sm">{p.size}</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-0.5">{p.dims}</div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
          <a href="/paper-size/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:underline">
            Explore Paper Size Tools →
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- ISO 9407 -->
        <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-canvas border border-hairline-soft">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
            <div>
              <span class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent text-[11px] font-semibold mb-2">ISO Standard</span>
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">ISO 9407 — Mondopoint Shoe Sizing</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="text-3xl flex-shrink-0">👟</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
            ISO 9407 defines the Mondopoint system, which expresses shoe sizes in millimeters of foot length and width. It is used in Japan, Korea, Russia, and by many military and safety footwear standards. Most consumer shoe markets use derivative systems (EU, US, UK) that can be converted back to Mondopoint.
          </p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-3 sm:grid-cols-6 gap-3 mb-4">
            {[
              { system: 'US Men', example: '9 US' },
              { system: 'US Women', example: '9 US' },
              { system: 'EU', example: '42 EU' },
              { system: 'UK', example: '8 UK' },
              { system: 'JP/CM', example: '27 cm' },
              { system: 'Mondopoint', example: '270 mm' },
            ].map((s) => (
              <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft text-center">
                <div class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-text-faint mb-1">{s.system}</div>
                <div class="font-bold text-ink text-sm">{s.example}</div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
          <a href="/shoe-size/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:underline">
            Explore Shoe Size Tools →
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- ASTM International -->
        <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-canvas border border-hairline-soft">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
            <div>
              <span class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent text-[11px] font-semibold mb-2">ASTM Standard</span>
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">ASTM International — US Apparel Sizing</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="text-3xl flex-shrink-0">👕</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
            ASTM International (formerly the American Society for Testing and Materials) publishes the primary standards for clothing sizes in the United States. Key standards include <strong class="text-ink">ASTM D5585</strong> (women's wear), <strong class="text-ink">ASTM D6240</strong> (men's wear), and <strong class="text-ink">ASTM D6192</strong> (children's wear).
          </p>
          <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
            US clothing sizes use a numerical system (XS, S, M, L, XL, or numeric 0–18 for women, 28–44 for men's waist) based on body measurements in inches. Our tools convert these to European (EN 13402), UK, and other regional systems.
          </p>
          <a href="/clothing-size/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:underline">
            Explore Clothing Size Tools →
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- EN 13402 -->
        <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-canvas border border-hairline-soft">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
            <div>
              <span class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent text-[11px] font-semibold mb-2">European Standard</span>
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">EN 13402 — European Clothing Sizes</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="text-3xl flex-shrink-0">🇪🇺</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
            EN 13402 is the European standard for size labeling of clothing, based on body measurements in centimeters. It replaced the older national standards across EU member states. The system uses primary dimensions (bust, waist, hip, height) to define size categories.
          </p>
          <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A typical European women's size 38 corresponds roughly to US size 8/10 and UK size 12. Men's EU sizes correspond to chest or waist measurements in centimeters.
          </p>
          <a href="/clothing-size/international-clothing-sizes/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:underline">
            See International Size Charts →
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- JIS -->
        <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-canvas border border-hairline-soft">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
            <div>
              <span class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent text-[11px] font-semibold mb-2">Japanese Standard</span>
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">JIS S 5037 — Japanese Footwear Sizing</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="text-3xl flex-shrink-0">🇯🇵</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Japan uses a centimeter-based shoe sizing system (e.g., 26.0 cm, 26.5 cm) that directly measures foot length. This is one of the most intuitive systems globally, closely aligned with the Mondopoint standard. Japanese sizes are the same for men and women — only the width designator (2E, 3E, 4E) changes.
          </p>
          <a href="/shoe-size/cm-to-shoe-size/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:underline">
            Try CM to Shoe Size Converter →
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Ring Standards -->
        <div class="p-8 rounded-3xl bg-canvas border border-hairline-soft">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
            <div>
              <span class="inline-flex items-center px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent text-[11px] font-semibold mb-2">Jewelry Standard</span>
              <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">Ring Sizing Systems</h2>
            </div>
            <span class="text-3xl flex-shrink-0">💍</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ring sizes vary significantly by region. The US/Canada system uses numbers 1–13 based on inner circumference in units of 1/16 of an inch. The UK/Australia system uses letters (A–Z+). Europe uses inner circumference in millimeters. Japan uses a numeric scale similar to the US but offset.
          </p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 mb-4">
            {[
              { system: 'US / Canada', example: 'Size 7' },
              { system: 'UK / Australia', example: 'Size N' },
              { system: 'EU / France', example: '54 mm' },
              { system: 'Japan', example: 'Size 13' },
            ].map((s) => (
              <div class="p-3 rounded-xl bg-canvas-soft text-center">
                <div class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-text-faint mb-1">{s.system}</div>
                <div class="font-bold text-ink text-sm">{s.example}</div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
          <a href="/ring-size/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:underline">
            Explore Ring Size Charts →
          </a>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Footer nav -->
    <div class="pt-8 border-t border-hairline-soft flex flex-wrap gap-6 text-sm text-text-muted">
      <a href="/about/" class="hover:text-ink transition-colors">← About Us</a>
      <a href="/privacy/" class="hover:text-ink transition-colors">Privacy Policy</a>
      <a href="/terms/" class="hover:text-ink transition-colors">Terms of Service</a>
    </div>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>
